# The tocdir/toeexpand expansion tree committed to this repo (tox/).
#
# `.text` (Text DAT body) and `.table` (Table DAT cells) files carry a
# binary length-prefixed preamble with embedded NUL bytes (see
# rootnotez/toetools docs/FORMAT.md), so git treats them as opaque binary and
# `git diff` / `git log -p` show only "Binary files differ" — hiding the
# most important content in the tree (e.g. td_snapshot/core.text, the
# snapshot script's own source). Route them through the toetools textconv
# renderer instead (`toetools textconv <file>`).
#
# textconv commands live in `.git/config`, which is not committed — run
# scripts/git-textconv-setup.sh once per clone to configure the driver
# (`diff.tocdir.textconv`) before this attribute has any visible effect;
# without it git falls back to its normal binary-file handling.
#
# `-text` disables git's own text/EOL handling on every file in these
# trees (not just .text/.table) so no autocrlf/renormalization can ever
# corrupt the length-prefixed binary framing tocdir round-trips bit-exact.

tox/**/*.text diff=tocdir
tox/**/*.table diff=tocdir
tox/** -text
